---
layout: layouts/identity.njk
permalink: /identity/
title: Foundations
description: Colour, typography, spacing and surface tokens for the Teenaz Spa visual identity.
---

<section class="section section--lg">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="stack--lg stack" style="max-width: 52rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule reveal" data-reveal>Visual identity</p>
      <h1 class="display-1 reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        A warm, intimate <em>urban sanctuary</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2" style="max-width: 52ch;">
        The system below defines how the brand looks and behaves — colour, type, spacing,
        components, imagery and motion. Every word on these pages is placeholder text.
        Content is decided separately.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<nav class="subnav" aria-label="On this page">
  <div class="shell">
    <ul class="subnav__list">
      <li><a class="subnav__link" href="#atmosphere">Atmosphere</a></li>
      <li><a class="subnav__link" href="#colour">Colour</a></li>
      <li><a class="subnav__link" href="#contrast">Contrast</a></li>
      <li><a class="subnav__link" href="#type">Typography</a></li>
      <li><a class="subnav__link" href="#space">Spacing</a></li>
      <li><a class="subnav__link" href="#surface">Surfaces</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

<!-- ── Atmosphere ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section" id="atmosphere" aria-labelledby="atmosphere-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">01 — Atmosphere</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="atmosphere-t">What the brand feels like</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        Every decision in this system is measured against these two lists. When a choice
        could go either way, the one that reads calmer and quieter wins.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="do-dont">
      <div class="do-dont__col do-dont__col--do reveal" data-reveal>
        <p class="do-dont__title">It should feel</p>
        <ul class="do-dont__list">
          {% for word in identity.atmosphere.is %}<li>{{ word }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="do-dont__col do-dont__col--dont reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        <p class="do-dont__title">It must never feel like</p>
        <ul class="do-dont__list">
          {% for word in identity.atmosphere.isNot %}<li>{{ word }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Colour ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--raised" id="colour" aria-labelledby="colour-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">02 — Colour</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="colour-t">Six colours, held in proportion</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        The ratio matters more than the colours themselves. Ivory and soft white carry the
        page; espresso carries the type; sand, sage and bronze appear in small, deliberate
        amounts. Bronze is a detail colour — warm and understated, never metallic or glossy.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Proportion bar: the 60/20/10/5/5 split, drawn to scale. -->
    <div class="spec" style="margin-bottom: var(--s-8);">
      <p class="spec__label">Distribution across a page</p>
      <div style="display: flex; height: 3.5rem; border-radius: var(--r-sm); overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line-quiet);">
        <div style="flex: 60; background: {{ identity.core.ivory }};"></div>
        <div style="flex: 20; background: {{ identity.core.espresso }};"></div>
        <div style="flex: 10; background: {{ identity.core.sand }};"></div>
        <div style="flex: 5; background: {{ identity.core.sage }};"></div>
        <div style="flex: 5; background: {{ identity.core.bronze }};"></div>
      </div>
      <p class="spec__note">
        60% ivory and soft white · 20% espresso · 10% sand · 5% sage · 5% bronze
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3">
      {% for colour in identity.palette %}
      <div class="swatch reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="{{ loop.index }}">
        <div class="swatch__chip" style="background: {{ colour.hex }};"></div>
        <div class="stack--sm stack">
          <div class="spec__label" style="border: 0; padding: 0;">
            <span class="swatch__name">{{ colour.name }}</span>
            <span class="ratio ratio--{{ colour.onIvoryGrade.level }}">{{ colour.share }}</span>
          </div>
          <p class="swatch__meta">{{ colour.hex }} · <code>{{ colour.token }}</code></p>
          <p class="swatch__role">{{ colour.role }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Derived tints ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="derived-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">02b — Derived tints</p>
      <h2 class="h2" id="derived-t">Four extensions, each earning its place</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        The six brand colours are the identity. These four are working tints derived from
        them, added because two of the brand colours cannot legally carry small text. They
        never appear as large fields of colour — only as type and borders.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-2">
      {% for tint in identity.derived %}
      <div class="card card--sand reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="{{ loop.index }}">
        <div class="card__body">
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-4);">
            <span style="width: 3rem; height: 3rem; border-radius: var(--r-sm); background: {{ tint.hex }}; flex: none;"></span>
            <div>
              <p class="h4">{{ tint.name }}</p>
              <p class="swatch__meta">{{ tint.hex }} · <code>{{ tint.token }}</code> · from {{ tint.from }}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="card__text">{{ tint.why }}</p>
          <p><span class="ratio ratio--{{ tint.onIvoryGrade.level }}">{{ tint.onIvory }}:1 on ivory — {{ tint.onIvoryGrade.label }}</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Contrast ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--alt" id="contrast" aria-labelledby="contrast-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">03 — Contrast</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="contrast-t">Which pairings are allowed</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        Measured, not estimated. Every ratio below is calculated from the hex values at
        build time, so this table cannot drift from the palette. AA is the minimum for any
        text a visitor has to read.
      </p>
    </header>

    {#
      tabindex makes the scroll container reachable by keyboard — without it,
      someone navigating without a mouse cannot scroll the table sideways.

      data-axe-ignore marks this block as exempt from the automated contrast
      audit, and only this block. The samples below deliberately render failing
      combinations so the rule can be seen rather than just described; flagging
      them would be the checker doing its job on content that exists to fail.
    #}
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;" tabindex="0" role="region"
         aria-label="Colour pairing contrast table" data-axe-ignore>
      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; min-width: 40rem;">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" style="text-align: left; padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-4) var(--s-3) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: var(--t-label); letter-spacing: var(--ls-label); text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 600;">Sample</th>
            <th scope="col" style="text-align: left; padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-4) var(--s-3) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: var(--t-label); letter-spacing: var(--ls-label); text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 600;">Ratio</th>
            <th scope="col" style="text-align: left; padding: var(--s-3) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: var(--t-label); letter-spacing: var(--ls-label); text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 600;">Where it may be used</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for pair in identity.pairings %}
          <tr>
            <td style="padding: var(--s-4) var(--s-4) var(--s-4) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-quiet);">
              <span style="display: inline-block; padding: var(--s-2) var(--s-4); border-radius: var(--r-xs); background: {{ pair.bgHex }}; color: {{ pair.fgHex }}; white-space: nowrap;">
                {{ pair.fg }}
              </span>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: var(--s-4) var(--s-4) var(--s-4) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-quiet); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;">
              <span class="ratio ratio--{{ pair.grade.level }}">{{ pair.ratio }}:1 · {{ pair.grade.label }}</span>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: var(--s-4) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-quiet); font-size: var(--t-small); color: var(--text-muted);">
              {{ pair.use }}
            </td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Typography ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section" id="type" aria-labelledby="type-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">04 — Typography</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="type-t">Cormorant Garamond and Manrope</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        Cormorant Garamond sets every editorial statement, at light weights and large
        sizes where its high contrast reads as composure rather than decoration. Manrope
        handles everything a visitor operates — navigation, buttons, labels, running copy.
        Nothing else is introduced.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom: var(--s-9);">
      <div class="card reveal" data-reveal>
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="eyebrow">Display face</p>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); font-weight: 300; line-height: 1;">Aa</p>
          <p class="h4">Cormorant Garamond</p>
          <p class="card__text">Light 300 · Regular 400 · Medium 500 · Semibold 600 · Italic</p>
          <p class="card__text">Headings and large editorial statements only. Never below about 20px, where its thin strokes lose definition.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="eyebrow">Interface face</p>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-ui); font-size: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); font-weight: 300; line-height: 1;">Aa</p>
          <p class="h4">Manrope</p>
          <p class="card__text">Light 300 · Regular 400 · Medium 500 · Semibold 600 · Bold 700</p>
          <p class="card__text">Body copy, navigation, buttons, form labels and any small heading inside an interface block.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="spec">
      <p class="spec__label">
        The scale
        <span class="spec__note">Display sizes are fluid between mobile and desktop; interface sizes are fixed so controls stay predictable.</span>
      </p>
      {% for step in identity.typeScale %}
      <div class="scale-row">
        <p class="{{ step.cls }}" style="margin: 0;">{{ step.sample }}</p>
        <div class="scale-row__meta">
          <span><strong>{{ step.name }}</strong></span>
          <span><code>{{ step.token }}</code></span>
          <span>{{ step.size }}</span>
          <span>{{ step.face }}</span>
        </div>
        <p class="spec__note">{{ step.use }}</p>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Spacing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--raised" id="space" aria-labelledby="space-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">05 — Spacing</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="space-t">Space is the luxury</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        More than any single colour or typeface, the generosity of the spacing is what
        makes this feel premium. Sections breathe at
        <code>clamp(4.5rem, 10vw, 9rem)</code>, and no viewport should carry more than one
        idea. If a screen feels busy, remove something rather than tightening the gaps.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="spec" style="margin-bottom: var(--s-8);">
      <p class="spec__label">Scale</p>
      {% for step in identity.spaceScale %}
      <div class="space-row">
        <code class="small">{{ step.token }}</code>
        <span class="swatch__meta">{{ step.px }}px</span>
        <div class="space-row__bar">
          <span class="space-bar" style="width: {{ step.px }}px;"></span>
          <span class="small muted space-row__use">{{ step.use }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card card--sand">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="h4">Container</p>
          <p class="card__text">
            Content is capped at <code>1280px</code> with a fluid gutter of
            <code>clamp(1.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem)</code>. A narrow variant at <code>940px</code>
            is used for long-form reading.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card--sand">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="h4">Measure</p>
          <p class="card__text">
            Running copy is capped at 62 characters, leads at 46. Short lines are part of
            the editorial feel and the main reason the pages read calmly on mobile.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Surfaces ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section" id="surface" aria-labelledby="surface-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">06 — Surfaces</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="surface-t">Corners, edges and depth</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        Rounding is restrained and shadows are almost absent. Elevation is communicated by
        a change of surface colour and a hairline border, not by float.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="spec">
        <p class="spec__label">Corner radius</p>
        <div class="stack">
          {% for r in identity.radii %}
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-4);">
            <span style="width: 4rem; height: 3rem; background: var(--sand); border-radius: {{ r.value }}; flex: none;"></span>
            <div>
              <p class="small"><code>{{ r.token }}</code> · {{ r.value }}</p>
              <p class="small muted">{{ r.use }}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="spec">
        <p class="spec__label">Elevation</p>
        <div class="stack">
          {% for s in identity.shadows %}
          <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s-4);">
            <span style="width: 4rem; height: 3rem; background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--line-quiet); border-radius: var(--r-md); box-shadow: {{ s.value }}; flex: none;"></span>
            <div>
              <p class="small"><code>{{ s.token }}</code></p>
              <p class="small muted">{{ s.use }}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
